Z||000000||sqoach||11-23-2000||09:47 PM||||does any1 know if IRM is still in business?  what's their online addy?  and has any1 had experience with them?<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||2
Z||000001||MrPBody||11-23-2000||10:23 PM||||As of a month or two ago, they were alive and well.  IRM has no web site, but here is a scanned copy of an out-of-date catalog<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html</A> <P>E-mail is IRMFIERO@aol.com<P>I have not ordered from them.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-23-2000||10:32 PM||||IRM is still in business. The only problem is ordering body parts. Anything made out of fiberglass takes a while to get (6-12 weeks)<BR>unless they have them on the shelf. All other items aren't to bad to get. (about 2 weeks)||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||11-24-2000||10:25 AM||||I have had several pleasant experiences with IRM. Before I moved to SC, I lived in MD, and would just go to IRM to buy stuff. Barbrah would always take the time to take me on a tour of their shop, showing me all the kit cars, Fieros, V6 engines, parts, making me drool all over the place. She almost let me drive her GT with the 3.1 installed. I've been on waiting lists for items, and recieved them quickly. The owner, Jim Sutter has called me long-distance several times to talk with me about my Fiero, which they installed the turbo on. Both Jim and Barbrah remember my Fiero, even though it was several years ago, and claim it as "the only black turbo-charged automatic 86SE in MD."<P>I'd buy anything from them, just give it a little time, I believe it's one person running the show.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||11-24-2000||05:06 PM||||IRMs Integrated Rocker Panels are definitely in my future.  As a matter of fact, I may just give up lowering springs for now just so I can get them.  I can always get lowering springs in the, er...spring.  Anyone know how the IRPs mount??  Adhesive?  Bolt on??  Direct replacement for???||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||11-25-2000||02:41 AM||||direct replacement bolt-on, AFAIK.. but I'd suggest asking Archie, he's done at least 2 cars with them..<P>and the next time you talk with IRM, can you ask if they've had time to consider my offer?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>tell them I'll throw in a domain name for free....<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000006||Monkeyman||11-26-2000||12:05 AM||||Steve--I've emailed them a few times but haven't heard anything back yet.  I keep meaning to call but I spend most of my time at work (went in at 4am this morning and just got home).||||reg||1
Z||000007||RNGCRSH||11-26-2000||12:52 PM||||They are still in business. They are also listed in "The Big Fiero Parts Book" available at  <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com" TARGET=_blank>CyberCars.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>"Fear" The sand in the machinery of life.<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 11-26-2000).]||||reg||10
